Track 3: Why Did You Erase the County Line?
- Story & Context: The EP concludes with the myth of the lost cartographer of San Gorgonio Pass, a bureaucrat who burned his survey logs and fled into the scrub with only a battery-powered monosynth and a mandolin. The track alternates between peaceful, glassy New Age drone washes and sudden explosions of hyper-fast, gothic bluegrass picking that mimic the sound of horse hooves galloping along a perimeter fence that no longer exists. During the climax, four scavenged synthesizers are cranked to self-oscillation until their cooling fans stall out and the sound snaps like severed wire. "The maps went blind before the chorus died," sings the choir of caravan elders, their harmonies thick and raspy over the final shudder of Chen's lowest cello string.
